    <briefdescription>
<para>Static-method namespace bridging engine <computeroutput><ref refid="class_matrix" kindref="compound">Matrix</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput>vec</computeroutput> values and the resolution engine&apos;s <computeroutput><ref refid="class_res_polynomial" kindref="compound">ResPolynomial</ref></computeroutput> representation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Resolution-side counterpart of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_f4to_m2_interface" kindref="compound">F4toM2Interface</ref></computeroutput>: every method is <computeroutput>static</computeroutput>. Provides <computeroutput><ref refid="class_res_f4to_m2_interface_acc204e41c5b849dbddd230a5c121f070_1acc204e41c5b849dbddd230a5c121f070" kindref="member">from_M2_vec</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_res_f4to_m2_interface_a415999e709aee01dbad7f071b9f0a00f_1a415999e709aee01dbad7f071b9f0a00f" kindref="member">to_M2_vec</ref></computeroutput> and the matrix-wide variants used by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_f4_res_computation" kindref="compound">F4ResComputation</ref></computeroutput> when handing input to the <computeroutput><ref refid="class_schreyer_frame" kindref="compound">SchreyerFrame</ref></computeroutput> and reading the resulting <computeroutput><ref refid="class_res_polynomial" kindref="compound">ResPolynomial</ref></computeroutput> syzygies back into engine-side <computeroutput>vec</computeroutput>s and <computeroutput>Matrix*</computeroutput>es for the front end. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
